    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0418" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1036: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-07T17:00:00+02:00">August 7, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 7—2:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5177. Department’s 4719, August 5, 5 p.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d420-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office states that in about a week a note will be sent by it to the
                    United Nations, <pb facs="0419" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/> suggesting a meeting of
                    United Nations representatives to prepare details for the setting up of the
                    Commission for the Investigation of War Crimes. Foreign Office believes, and
                    this seems reasonable to us, that a month or 6 weeks will elapse before this
                    meeting will take place. Until this meeting takes place it is difficult for us
                    to say anything helpful regarding the probable date when the proposed Commission
                    will begin functioning.</p>
                <p>We shall, of course, immediately inform the Department of the substance of the
                    note mentioned above.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d420-f1" n="13" xml:id="d420-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it inquired as to the status of negotiations and probable date on
                    which Mr. Pell’s presence in London would be required (740.00116
                    E.W.1939/991).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
